<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarke-modal-system">
  <metadata>
    <title>P1 — Window controls into Compose/AI.Widgets/SpaarkeAi dialogs — FR-12</title>
    <phase>1 Window-controls rollout</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 003</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modify-only rollout across existing dialogs outside `Spaarke.UI.Components` (no new public surface); each keeps its behavior — only the maximize/restore + × cluster is standardized.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Repetitive shared-lib/code-page component edits, fully specified by the shipped `ModalWindowControls` primitive and an explicit dialog list.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>003</deps>
    <tags>react, fluent-ui, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Roll the reconciled `ModalWindowControls` (Dataverse `FullScreenMaximize/Minimize` glyph + ×, from task 003) into the non-`Spaarke.UI.Components` dialogs via the same interim header adapter used in task 030 (FR-12): `Spaarke.Compose.Components/.../ComposeConflictDialog.tsx`, `Spaarke.AI.Widgets/.../memory/PinnedMemoryEditDialog.tsx`, `.../memory/PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation.tsx`, and `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/.../conversation/QuickStartModal.tsx`. Verify that `CommunicationConversationPanel/.../ConversationModal.tsx` ALREADY consumes `ModalWindowControls` and skip it. Preserve each dialog's existing behavior, messaging, props, and size EXACTLY — standardize only the window-control cluster.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Fluent UI v9 dialog composition across shared libs and code pages. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The four listed dialogs render the shared `ModalWindowControls` (FullScreen maximize/restore + ×) in their headers with behavior unchanged; `ConversationModal` is verified as already-consuming and left untouched; `Spaarke.Compose.Components`, `Spaarke.AI.Widgets`, and the SpaarkeAi Code Page all build green under `@types/react` 18 and React 19.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>P1 spans every custom dialog, not just those in `Spaarke.UI.Components`. Task 030 covers the UI.Components set; this task covers the Compose lib, the AI.Widgets memory dialogs, and the SpaarkeAi `QuickStartModal`. `ConversationModal` (in the CommunicationConversationPanel PCF) already consumes `ModalWindowControls` per project discovery — it is verified here, not re-wired (its full replacement is P5). `QuickStartModal` lives in `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/**`, a declared hot-path surface.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeConflictDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/components/memory/PinnedMemoryEditDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/components/memory/PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/QuickStartModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/ModalWindowControls/ModalWindowControls.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/pcf/CommunicationConversationPanel/CommunicationConversationPanel/ConversationModal.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Reconciled `ModalWindowControls` (FullScreen glyph + ×) — the primitive this task drops into each header.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Consume the single shared `ModalWindowControls` from `@spaarke/ui-components`; do NOT copy its markup into each dialog or fork a per-lib control cluster.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Header edits use semantic tokens only — zero hex, `'1px'` literals, or inline color styles introduced in any touched dialog (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Compose the existing primitive — MUST NOT fork `ModalWindowControls`. Preserve each dialog's existing behavior (incl. `ComposeConflictDialog`/`PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation` non-dismissible alert semantics), messaging, props, and size; standardize ONLY the maximize/restore + × cluster.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SpaarkeAi is a declared hot-path (`QuickStartModal` under `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/**`) — run `/conflict-check` and cite it before opening any PR that touches SpaarkeAi.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">All touched files MUST compile clean under `@types/react` 18 (PCF) and React 19 (Code Pages) — NFR-04.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Fluent v9 dialog header composition + window controls (cross-lib)</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SHARED-UI-COMPONENTS-GUIDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-component-authoring" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md">Shared-lib header/slot conventions.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-12 + design §6.4 + task 030's interim adapter approach + the shipped `ModalWindowControls`. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD.</step>
    <step order="1">Verify `CommunicationConversationPanel/.../ConversationModal.tsx` already consumes `ModalWindowControls` and shows the reconciled glyph after task 003; record the verification and do NOT modify it.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire the cluster into `Spaarke.Compose.Components/.../ComposeConflictDialog.tsx`, preserving its non-dismissible alert behavior and 3-button footer.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire the cluster into `Spaarke.AI.Widgets/.../memory/PinnedMemoryEditDialog.tsx` and `.../PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation.tsx`, preserving their edit/delete semantics and messaging.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the cluster into `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/.../conversation/QuickStartModal.tsx`, preserving its quick-start behavior; run `/conflict-check` for the SpaarkeAi hot-path before the PR.</step>
    <step order="5">Build `Spaarke.Compose.Components`, `Spaarke.AI.Widgets`, and the SpaarkeAi Code Page; prove dual-React cleanliness; fix any type breaks.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the ui-tests below (controls present per dialog + dark-mode parity).</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 031 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document the `ConversationModal` verification result and any non-mechanical adaptation in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If `ConversationModal` is found NOT to consume `ModalWindowControls` (contradicting discovery), or if a dialog's alert/non-dismissible contract cannot host the cluster without behavior change, STOP and surface it per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than adapting silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Standard controls present on the four converted dialogs">
      <steps>
        <step>Open `ComposeConflictDialog`, `PinnedMemoryEditDialog`, `PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation`, and `QuickStartModal` in a harness/consumer.</step>
        <step>Confirm the FullScreen maximize/restore glyph + × render and behave; confirm alert dialogs still block ESC/backdrop dismissal.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All four show the standard `ModalWindowControls` cluster; alert/non-dismissible semantics preserved; prior behavior unchanged.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark-mode parity (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render `ComposeConflictDialog` and `QuickStartModal` under the dark Fluent theme.</step>
        <step>Verify controls + header border read correctly via semantic tokens in both light and dark.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Correct light/dark contrast via semantic tokens; no hex/inline color introduced.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test shared libs and the SpaarkeAi code page (build:prod for PCF)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeConflictDialog.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/components/memory/PinnedMemoryEditDialog.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/components/memory/PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/QuickStartModal.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given each of `ComposeConflictDialog`, `PinnedMemoryEditDialog`, `PinnedMemoryDeleteConfirmation`, and `QuickStartModal`, when opened, then its header renders the FullScreen maximize/restore + × cluster from the shared `ModalWindowControls`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `ConversationModal`, then it is verified to already consume `ModalWindowControls` (shows the FullScreen glyph after task 003) and is left unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each converted dialog's prior behavior, messaging, props, size, and alert/non-dismissible semantics are unchanged; only the window-control cluster is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no dialog introduces a new hex value, `'1px'` literal, or inline color style; no fork/copy of `ModalWindowControls` is created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Spaarke.Compose.Components`, `Spaarke.AI.Widgets`, and the SpaarkeAi Code Page build green; `/conflict-check` was run for the SpaarkeAi PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>CLAUDE.md "Key Facts" confirm `ConversationModal` already uses `ModalWindowControls` (createPortal + position:fixed; full replacement deferred to P5). `QuickStartModal` re-base to `FormModal` is P3 (task in that phase) — this task only adds the window controls. COMPLETED 2026-08-01 (parallel sub-agent, STANDARD rigor): 4/4 dialogs wired via `DialogTitle action` slot; alert/non-dismissible semantics preserved (× → existing onCancel/handleCancel only); ConversationModal verified already-consuming (`@spaarke/ui-components` barrel + React-16 boundary cast) and untouched. Builds: Compose.Components + AI.Widgets + full SpaarkeAi (4019 modules + ribbon) green; 4 sibling dists built en route. Tests: SpaarkeAi 838/838; AI.Widgets 677/678 and Compose 843/858 (failures pre-existing, git-stash A/B-proven). Conflict-check: soft-pass (zero open-PR overlap). Detail: notes/task-031-completion.md.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge/files first. Follow task-execute.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
